<title>AUSTRIA: AUSTRIAN ARILINES EXTENDS SAFRICA SERVICE.</title>
<headline>AUSTRIAN ARILINES EXTENDS SAFRICA SERVICE.</headline>
<dateline>VIENNA 1997-02-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Austrian Airlines AG announced on Monday it will increase its weekly flights to Johannesburg to three from two at the start of the 1997 European summer flight schedule.</p>
<p>The airline also said in a statement flights currently scheduled to Johannesburg on Mondays and Wednesdays would be extended to Cape Town from May 19. The airline's new long distance jet, Airbus A340-300 -- which has a seating capacity of 297 -- would be used for the route, it added.</p>
</text>
